body:
`SufrFile::suffix_search` in `libsufr/src/sufr_file.rs` runs each query on rayon and collects the results like this:

```rust
.flat_map(|(query_num, query)| -> Result<SearchResult<T>> {
    let mut search = thread_local_search.get_or_try(new_search)?.borrow_mut();
    search.search(query_num, &query, args.find_suffixes)
})
.collect();
```

`Result` implements `IntoParallelIterator`. An `Ok` yields one item and an `Err` yields none. A query whose `SufrSearch` construction or `search` call fails therefore disappears from the returned `Vec`, and `suffix_search` still returns `Ok`. `count`, `extract` and `locate` all go through `suffix_search`, so a caller of any of them gets fewer results than queries and no error.

Found by reading the code. Not reproduced.
